            "accordion_row_Lgiq6Q": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "name": "t:names.accordion_row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "How does the MinerForge Pro actually work?",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text_VgfGpw": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "name": "t:names.text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>The MinerForge Pro connects to the Bitcoin network and performs real solo mining - meaning it independently tries to find a valid block hash. It uses open, read-only network data to participate safely in the mining process without accessing your personal information or wallet.<br/><br/>Each “shot” is a new attempt at discovering a block, which theoretically could yield a Bitcoin reward, although the odds are very small.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "none",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "color": "var(--color-foreground)",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 0,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text_VgfGpw"
              ]
            },
            "accordion_row_7j7ewC": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "name": "t:names.accordion_row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "Does buying more miners improve my odds?",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text_rPUXVd": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "name": "t:names.text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>Yes. Each device runs independently, producing its own stream of hashes (lottery tickets). The more units you run, the more chances you have of hitting a winning block.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "none",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
